  "goodToKnow": "Die Vergänglichkeit is transience or impermanence: die Vergänglichkeit des Lebens, der Schönheit. It was a central theme of German Baroque poetry, written amid the devastation of the Thirty Years' War, and of vanitas paintings with skulls and wilting flowers. Vergänglich means transient; vergehen means to pass. The opposite is die Ewigkeit (eternity). It has no plural."
